Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Cover retry custody review branches and preserve
 interrupt issuer

Problem: restored retry waits label a backend-exit interrupt as user Stop; independent review also found five untested custody clauses. Why: the new pre-provider exception branch hardcoded user attribution, while earlier tests asserted only terminal provider timing. Root happened: attribution was not preserved at the new interrupt boundary. Root not caught: redundant wait gates masked ordering and guard mutations. Recurrence: scoped follow-up to PR3820 review6001906830, not a new natural-window receipt. Countermeasures: use the canonical interrupt issuer; seven focused cases kill all six mutations including Stop during boundary, declined wait return, per-iteration ordering, refused-marker carry and stale exact-value clear. Proof: r22-mutants.log baseline7pass,6killed; regression38pass/10files; scripts/check21OK. Real600s process proof remains prior r20 evidence, not rerun or installed proof here. Actual-precondition installed verification and5natural90s windows remain verifier-owned; historical latency failures are not waived.
